; Doc 01 §6.1's tree, and nothing else. Every rest position, every anchor offset
; and the shadow's points are DERIVED from the CharacterProportions resource by
; rig_humanoid.gd — a number authored here would be a number an inheriting
; character scene could not override with §10's one field.
;
; §10: this is an inherited-scene BASE. dipper.tscn (row 1.3) and the other 30+
; character scenes inherit it, which is also why the root is a CharacterBody2D
; rather than §6.1's Node2D — see the deviation note in rig_humanoid.gd.
;
; The b_hair_01 → b_hair_02 → b_hair_03 chain §6.1 marks "(Wendy/Mabel only)" is
; deliberately ABSENT: an inherited scene adds nodes freely, and every other
; character would otherwise carry three bones no animation ever touches.
;
; The two properties authored on every Bone2D are engine bookkeeping, not
; geometry — the script still overwrites `rest` with the derived pose:
;   * `rest` — Bone2D's constructor leaves `rest` an ALL-ZERO Transform2D as its
;     "no rest authored yet" sentinel, and Skeleton2D inverts every bone's rest
;     during bone setup, which happens on enter_tree, before `_ready()` can
;     derive one. An identity rest here is what keeps that from being 18
;     `affine_invert: det == 0` errors on every character in the game.
;   * `auto_calculate_length_and_angle = false` on the seven terminal bones — the
;     gizmo length is derived from a FIRST CHILD bone, and a leaf has none, so
;     every leaf warns on every instantiation otherwise. Note the spelling: the
;     accessors are `get_autocalculate_…`, the PROPERTY is `auto_calculate_…`,
;     and a text scene drops a misspelled property silently.

;
; PARTS. §6.2's z_index table is authored HERE and the geometry is derived in
; rig_humanoid.gd, for the reason Deferred R1 gives: real art lands by assigning
; a texture to these same nodes in the Inspector, and an artist cannot select a
; node that is conjured at runtime. Same for `color` — §9.2's placeholder fills,
; overridable per character, and the ONLY thing besides the proportions resource
; §10 lets an inheriting scene touch.
;
; `hair_back` (z 10) and `hair_front` (z 30) are deliberately ABSENT, exactly as
; the b_hair_01→03 chain above is: §6.1 marks the hair "(Wendy/Mabel only)", and
; an inherited scene adds nodes freely. Every other row of §6.2's table is here.

